  "evidence_tolerance": 2.0,
  "seed": 42,
  "note": "Bayesian evidence comparison for PDS 456 with nested sampling (UltraNest, speed=auto). Band is 2-10 keV, the canonical Fe K-alpha band: extending to 0.5 keV leaves an unmodelled soft-excess/cross-calibration residual that holds chi2/dof at 2.70, whereas 2-10 keV gives 1.73 and makes the line-vs-absorption comparison interpretable.  Priors: 25-start chi-square scans show a narrow line (sigma 50 eV) improves chi2 by 27, an unconstrained-width line by 162, and pcfabs by 158 - so the free-width line and the partial covering are degenerate competitors and both are sampled.  cutoffpl_cabs is dropped: it improves chi2 by only 2.6 for two extra parameters on 0.5-10 keV data, i.e. unidentifiable; a Compton-thick comparison needs broadband (NuSTAR) data.  MYTorus/UXCLUMPY/RELXILL tables are not bundled (licence/download gated). Fe K-alpha width is treated as two fixed hypotheses (50 eV narrow, 300 eV broad) instead of a free parameter: a free sigma is a flat likelihood direction, which drove the sampler to 0.04 % efficiency at 94 % of the evidence volume.",
